    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\n\nI don't know how to reproduce it but sometimes after couple of hours writing code with clangd LSP (which sometimes shows a notification) I get an error while trying to `:wall!`.\n\n<img width=\"1878\" height=\"210\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eedd077f-5f67-451a-86ba-160d66680c2e\" />\n\nThe buffer in question is impossible to find and not listed at all using `:ls`\n\nHowever if I type `:%bd` I get this error while the buffer does not seem to exist:\n\n<img width=\"922\" height=\"138\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd693174-2e95-485e-907b-3a2d45db2ac1\" />\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI try to figure out how to reproduce still.",
