        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> The buffer in question is impossible to find and not listed at all using `:ls`\n\nIt is a not listed helper buffer and it is possible to see it listed with `:ls!` (with a `!`). It should be possible to avoid the error when deleting buffers with `:%bd!` (again, with an `!`).\n\n---\n\nI indeed was able reproduce this by doing the following in a clean config:\n\n- `:lua require('mini.notify').setup()`\n- `:lua vim.notify('Hello')` followed by `:%bd` while notification is still visible.\n- Doing `:ls!` shows that the temporary 'mini.notify' buffer is still listed and modified.\n- Doing `:wall!` shows the error.\n\nI'll take a look.",
